# [OPT-5]/r48 F1: MULTI-CHAIN witnesses — patterns whose machines carry MORE
# scan-chain candidates than PCREC_MAX_SCAN_EDGES (4 per machine), so the
# selection cap's two sites (the pass's own conjunct, scanedge.c, and the
# emit-side annotation cap, emit_dfa.c) are both exercised with chains left
# OVER. Correct behavior either way the cap binds: unselected chains simply
# stay table-walked. Sabotage row S215 deletes the PASS-side conjunct and
# these cells are its detector. Expectations python3-re verified 2026-08-31.

# five counted single-class segments -> ~10 chain candidates across the
# forward machine ({m,n} splits at the accept transition), cap keeps 4
pattern [a-c]{2,4}[0-9]{2,4}[A-C]{2,4}[j-l]{2,4}[x-z]{2,4}
m "ab12ABjkxy" 0 10
m "abc123ABCjklxyz" 0 15
m "zzab12ABjkxyzz" 2 14
n "ab12ABjk"
n "ab12ABjkx"

# the unbounded-tail variant: four bounded chains + a * self-loop chain
pattern [a-c]{2,4}[0-9]{2,4}[A-C]{2,4}[j-l]{2,4}[x-z]*
m "ab12ABjk" 0 8
m "ab12ABjkxyz" 0 11
n "ab12AB"
